From 100aabba29e8f768a13cff6f5db0168916f2173c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Diller <dillera@dillernet.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:35:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] FujiNet floppy in the external drive, GCR tracks from the
 FujiNet

The FujiNet announces its floppy slot on the same link as the DCD chain
('s'/'d' inserted, 'u'/'l' writable, 'r' removed). The disk goes in the
external drive, behind the chain, built from GCR tracks the FujiNet
encodes ('#' cyl side). When the motor stops, tracks the Mac changed go
back whole ('P') for the FujiNet to decode; a Mac eject is sent as the
board's eject command ('7').

snow_floppy: FloppyImage::from_bitstreams and track_bitstream.
